Omission
- [N1] Omitted trace (input 1): i1:To start the process, begin by supplying the requirement and then documenting it. -> i2:If the order is received via fax -> i4:input the order into an Excel file -> i8:Once the Excel list is complete after a week, send it to the student. -> i10:Upon receiving the Excel list, type the orders into the MS-Access database. After typing the orders into the database, ensure that it is completed. -> i11:Once the database is completed, control the incoming order. At the same time, continue to do the check. -> i12:If the order is correct -> i13:If the order is correct, release it. -> i14:Send the Excel list to the student and upon receiving it, continue with the process. -> i17:If the order is worth less than 5.000 € -> i18:If the order is worth less than 5.000 €, release it. -> i23:Once the order is received by PPC, they will initiate production. -> i26:If the issue can be solved -> i27:If the issue can be solved, release the order. -> i28:After PPC initiates production, the goods will be produced.
- [N2] Omitted trace (input 3): i1:To start the process, begin by supplying the requirement and then documenting it. -> i2:If the order is received via fax -> i4:input the order into an Excel file -> i8:Once the Excel list is complete after a week, send it to the student. -> i10:Upon receiving the Excel list, type the orders into the MS-Access database. After typing the orders into the database, ensure that it is completed. -> i11:Once the database is completed, control the incoming order. At the same time, continue to do the check. -> i12:If the order is correct -> i13:If the order is correct, release it. -> i14:Send the Excel list to the student and upon receiving it, continue with the process. -> i17:If the order is worth less than 5.000 € -> i18:If the order is worth less than 5.000 €, release it. -> i23:Once the order is received by PPC, they will initiate production. -> i26:If the issue can be solved -> i27:If the issue can be solved, release the order. -> i28:After PPC initiates production, the goods will be produced. -> i30:If not, check the quality of the goods. Once the quality is checked, create and send a quality report to the finance department. -> i31:Release the order via memo and ensure that the memo is achieved in the warehouse. -> i33:At the same time, commission the goods and sign and send the memo. -> i35:Finally, archive the memo and close the order. This marks the end of the process.
